{
  "$id": "ooo.schema.v2",
  "title": "CAT OS Odd One Out content item, schema v2",
  "description": "Schema v2 = v1 plus the pattern layer of the content engine (content/taxonomy/varc-taxonomy.json): meta.reasoning_patterns names the discourse and reasoning patterns the item exercises, meta.genre widens to the thirty taxonomy genres, and meta.quality records the adversarial review and blind solve. v1 files remain valid under v1; versions are appended, never edited. Original v1 description: One Odd One Out item: five topically related sentences of which exactly four form a coherent paragraph and one must be excluded (ODD_MAN_OUT_BIBLE TL;DR). The design axis is the Bible's single most important principle: the outlier is ON TOPIC but OUT OF STRUCTURE, defined by the discourse relation it cannot enter, never by the topic it is about (Bible §4). The metadata implements Bible §13: the seven way violation taxonomy (§4 a to g), the difficulty vector with topical_overlap as the primary lever (§6), the two engineered traps (§5, Trap A = a belonging sentence looks odd, Trap B = the outlier looks like it belongs), cohesion signals per Halliday and Hasan tie (§3), the bounded Reading DNA extension (§8, exactly four new traits plus two inherited), and the §11 validation gates (uniqueness, reconstruction, heuristic adversarial, trap audit) which must all pass before an item ships. The explanation implements §12: reconstruct the core paragraph, assign each core sentence its discourse role and name the ties, name the precise structural principle the outlier violates, and expose the trap. exclusion_analysis tags every core sentence with the §7 solver pattern that makes it tempting to exclude, so a learner's exact pick powers precise Reading DNA diagnosis. Format facts (five sentences, TITA, +3/0) are carried as configuration with a verification note, never as timeless fact (Bible §1, Recommendation 1). Validation subset: see src/core/content-loader/validator.js.",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "schema_version",
    "meta",
    "sentences",
    "outlier",
    "core_order",
    "builder",
    "explanation",
    "mentor"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "schema_version": {
      "const": 2
    },
    "meta": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "id",
        "type",
        "version",
        "status",
        "quality_score",
        "genre",
        "difficulty",
        "difficulty_numeric",
        "tier",
        "title",
        "theme",
        "estimated_time_sec",
        "format",
        "spine_type",
        "nucleus",
        "violation_type",
        "difficulty_vector",
        "traps",
        "cohesion_signals",
        "dna_traits",
        "mission",
        "validation",
        "learning_objective",
        "source",
        "date_added",
        "batch_id",
        "prompt_version",
        "reviewer_notes",
        "reasoning_patterns",
        "quality"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^ooo-[0-9]{4}$"
        },
        "type": {
          "const": "ooo"
        },
